Z||000008||sjp777||12-31-2001||09:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B>FieroLisa you are SO spoiled!!! HaHa<P>sjp777..<P>They look really nice..  I've been pondering about getting some.<BR>How did they go on.. easy, hard..???<BR>Do they keep their shape after sitting??<P>PS your door sills are red.. is that custom?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1st one took about 4 hours, second was easier. As long as you have the video, it's almost impossible to screw up.<P>They do retain shape nicely. the seats are even starting to mold to the shape of my ass.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Door sills are red stock from the factory. 88GT's had the monochrome paint||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dragon||12-31-2001||09:38 PM||||The wonderful thing abut Mr Mike's seats is that you do not have to have a great set of seats to start with.  When you order from him let him know if you have spots missing foam or what ever the problem and chances are he know what you need to do to fix it.<P>Or you can always come to the Daytona show and talk to Mike in person.  He is a great guy to talk to!!!<P>------------------<BR>Dragon<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://SpaceCoastFieros.com/edragon.jpg">  <BR>             <BR>   Space Coast Fieros -&gt; Florida Fiero Council<P>             Florida Fiero Weekend <A HREF="http://FloridaFieros.org/daytona2002" TARGET=_blank>http://FloridaFieros.org/daytona2002</A>||||reg||6
